---
title: M07 Implemented local counter lifecycle - volatile and cooperative
---
flowchart TB
    Submit["Authorized valid submit\nreserve and prepare\natomic record + intent + queue"]
    Queued["Queued\naccepted volatile receipt"]
    Running["Running\npermission and time checked\nbounded steps, yield preserves state"]
    Requested["Running, cancel requested\nreason: user or runtime budget\nyield keeps request pending\nnot a terminal state"]
    Success["Succeeded"]
    Failed["Failed\npolicy denial/unavailable before start\nor execution failure"]
    Cancelled["Cancelled\nnever started or confirmed stopped"]
    Expired["Expired\nqueue deadline; never started"]
    Submit --> Queued
    Queued --> Running
    Queued --> Cancelled
    Queued --> Expired
    Queued --> Failed
    Running --> Requested
    Running --> Success
    Running --> Failed
    Requested --> Cancelled
    Requested --> Success
    Requested --> Failed
    Note["Terminal states never restart.\nRepeated cancel returns AlreadyTerminal.\nRetention eviction is not an execution state.\nPanic or uncooperative step can invalidate host."]
    classDef pending fill:#fff1d6,stroke:#ae7b26,color:#163744;
    classDef terminal fill:#e8f4f7,stroke:#24576b,color:#163744;
    classDef note fill:#f1f3f6,stroke:#909aa8,color:#243342;
    class Submit,Queued,Running,Requested pending;
    class Success,Failed,Cancelled,Expired terminal;
    class Note note;
